+
+This is a private successor to the exact currently published four-case qualification. New inputs are exact corrected negative-controls V2 bytes; its V1 HOLD (NC1 incompatible channel-layout tag) is pinned and superseded only by the distinct V2 type tag. All future source review, publication and native execution remain separate. No tests/imports/build/native action occurred here. Head75c's consumed four-case actual result remains its original bounded scope; it supplies no passing prefix for these eight cases.
+
+Owner changes are limited to the exact new fixture protocol, six additional stage literals, eight ordered names, TRUNCATED_RIGHTS success stage and the conservative source hash multiplier4→8. Loader changes are only exact fixture/facade SHA literals. Acquisition/scan/ordinary sender are unchanged in the native component; finite test-only negative API and V2 tag are declared by that component.
+
+The same40s fixture,10s cleanup,150s inner total,1GiB selected+child hash cap and all stream/tool/header/archive/dependency caps remain. The source map now has eight Node processes: fixture, five direct targets, nested owner, nested target. Node image is hashed once, verified source set conservatively eight times and addon twice; overflow refuses. The old1024-byte canonical parser remains stricter than the component2048 upper ceiling. Result fields/protocol of the owner remain fixed; embedded fixture protocol/case/stage is deliberately new. UNKNOWN_HOLD remains nonterminal with retained originals; never restart authority.
+
+launch/entry/header/libc and metadata/custody helpers stay byte-identical. The actual seven ChildProcess children follow their original EOF/pipe lifecycle; the six external Python-owned stage originals remain retained WNOWAIT/reaped/EOF with no post-reap signal or global absence claim. Public source entry/platform/tool/library trust is unchanged. Selected-M preprocessing dependencies do not certify compiler frontend/assembler/linker/specs/startup/runtime distribution. Future same-job metadata/header/libc/source/artifact checks remain required.
+
+Admission template stays executionAdmitted=false and null future source/head/run/tool/output bindings. No production/provider credentials, recovery, Darwin idle policy, fleet/release/deploy approval is included. Private streams are exact<slot>.stdout/.stderr, never artifact wildcards. The only public transport file is result.json.
